# One decode step of a Llama-style model (Llama, Qwen3, Qwen3-MoE, gpt-oss, and
# DeepSeek-V3-style mixtures of experts on ordinary attention: GLM-4.5, dots.llm1) in a single
# call: token in, next token (greedy) out.
#
# Megakernel-style fusion for CPUs: every elementwise op runs inside the pass that produces
# or consumes its data, so a layer is 2 serial norms and 5 `par` regions:
#   1. RMSNorm + Q8 quantization of the input                (serial, d values)
#   2. Q/K/V projections + RoPE + KV-cache append              (par, one task per head)
#   3. attention: splits of 256 positions                     (par, per KV head and split)
#      merged per query head + Q8 quantization of its output     (par, one task per q head)
#   4. O projection + residual add                             (par, 64 rows per task)
#   5. RMSNorm + Q8 quantization                               (serial)
#   6. gate and up projections + SwiGLU + Q8 quantization      (par, 64 rows per task)
#   7. down projection + residual add                          (par, 64 rows per task)
# then the final RMSNorm and the LM head with a fused argmax: each task keeps only the best
# of its 64 logits, so the logits are never written.
#
# llama_prefill runs n prompt tokens through the same passes in one call: every projection
# task applies its weights to 8 tokens at a time (qmat_batch; 4 with 128-bit vectors), so a
# weight matrix is read once per 8 tokens rather than once per token; attention runs per
# token in tiles of 8, the splits all 8 see whole once for the tile's query heads; norms and
# epilogues run per token. Its results are exactly those of n llama_decode calls.
#
# Each weight matrix is Q8_0, Q4_0, Q6_K, Q4_K, Q5_K, Q4_1, IQ4_NL or MXFP4, chosen per
# matrix (and per part of a fused matrix: Q, K and V may differ): 8-, 4-, 6- or 5-bit
# weights with f16 scales per 32 (Q6_K: 16) values of a row (Q4_1 an f16 min too; IQ4_NL's
# and MXFP4's 4-bit codes index a codebook), or for Q4_K and Q5_K a 6-bit scale
# and min per 32 under f16 factors per 256, packed in chunks of 64 output rows; activations are quantized to int8 per 32-block on the fly and the int8 dots
# run on `vdotu` (weights stored unsigned; the activation sums of quantize_q8 remove their
# offset or apply the mins).
# The matrix chunks (qmat_chunk), the quantization, RoPE, softmax's exp (vexp, no libm call)
# and SwiGLU's gating come from the AIR standard library (`use`).
#
# Shapes: d, ffn and vocab multiples of 64; head_dim a multiple of 64; heads a multiple of
# kv_heads (grouped-query attention); pos < max_ctx.
#
# cfg (i64[17]): d, layers, heads, kv_heads, head_dim, ffn (the dense layers' MLP width),
# vocab, max_ctx, KV cache format (0 bf16, 1 int8), then for a mixture-of-experts model the
# experts, the experts each token uses, an expert's MLP width and how the used experts are
# picked and weighted (0 softmax probabilities, 1 those renormalized to sum to 1 (Qwen3-MoE),
# 2 a softmax of the picked logits (gpt-oss), 3 sigmoid probabilities picked with a selection
# bias and renormalized (GLM-4.5, dots.llm1), 4 the same not renormalized; 0s for a dense
# model), then the MLP's activation (0 SwiGLU, 1 gpt-oss's clamped SwiGLU), the rotary
# dimensions of a head (0 for all of head_dim; GLM-4.5 rotates half), the shared experts'
# MLP width (0 for none) and the routed experts' weight scale (an f32 in the low 4 bytes)
# model (table of 8-byte words): a matrix is a pointer to its parts, 4 words each: packed
# weights, scales, format (0: Q8_0, 1: Q4_0, 2: Q6_K, 3: Q4_K, 4: Q5_K, 5: Q4_1, 6: IQ4_NL,
# 7: MXFP4) and number of 64-row chunks (see qmat_chunk in the standard library). A vector
# (norm weights, biases) is a pointer to f32s, 0 where the model has none.
#   [0] token embedding f32 [vocab x d]   [1] final norm weight f32 [d]   [2] LM head
#   [vocab x d]   [3] RoPE cos f32 [max_ctx x rotary dims/2]   [4] RoPE sin (same shape;
#   RoPE scaling such as YaRN is in the tables)
#   then 18 per layer, at 5 + 18 * l:
#   attention norm f32 [d]; QKV [(heads + 2 kv_heads) * head_dim x d] (rows: all q heads,
#   then k heads, then v heads); O [d x heads * head_dim]; MLP norm f32 [d]; gate/up
#   [2 ffn x d], chunks interleaved (gate rows 64c.., then up rows 64c..); down [d x ffn];
#   Q and K norm weights f32 [head_dim] (Qwen3's RMSNorm of each q and k head before RoPE);
#   then for a mixture-of-experts layer (gate/up and down 0) its router [experts x d] and a
#   table of 4 words per expert: its gate/up [2 expert_ffn x d] and down [d x expert_ffn]
#   matrices and their biases (f32, gate/up's laid out as its rows) (0 and 0 for a dense
#   layer); then gpt-oss's biases of QKV [(heads + 2 kv_heads) * head_dim], O [d] and the
#   router [experts], its attention sinks f32 [heads] (a logit per query head that takes
#   part in the softmax with no value), and the layer's attention window in positions (a
#   query sees the last that many, itself included; 0 for all of them); then a
#   DeepSeek-style layer's shared expert, gate/up [2 shared_ffn x d] and down [d x
#   shared_ffn] (a dense MLP on the same input, added after the routed experts), and its
#   routed experts' selection bias f32 [experts] (0s for none). A mixture-of-experts model's
#   layers without a router are dense, ffn wide (GLM-4.5's and dots.llm1's first).
# cache: per layer, K then V, each kv_heads x ctx x head_dim bf16 values, ctx = max_ctx
# rounded up to a multiple of 32 (head-major, so a KV head's positions are contiguous): V is
# [kv_heads x ctx x head_dim]; K is in tiles of 32 positions, [kv_heads x ctx / 32 x
# head_dim x 32], so a vector holds one value of consecutive positions. Attention runs on
# the standard library's attn_split and attn_merge (flash-decoding): each 256-position split
# of a KV head is scored with positions in lanes (no horizontal sums) and mixed with V's
# columns in lanes, for the group's query heads 4 at a time, each K and V vector widened
# from bf16 once for the 4. An int8 cache (format 1) takes hd + 4 bytes per position
# instead of 2 hd: per KV head, tiles of 32 positions, each the int8 values (K's plus 128 in
# groups of 4 per position, [head_dim / 4 x 32 x 4]; V [32 x head_dim]) then an f32 scale per
# position (to_q8_kv); attn_split_q8 scores it with int8 dots (`vdotu`) on queries rounded
# to int8.
# A windowed layer whose window needs far fewer positions than the context keeps a ring
# instead (kv_ring): R = window + 31 + 256 slots rounded up to 32, position p at slot p mod R
# and again at p mod R + R, so its planes are 2 R slots per KV head rather than ctx; layers
# follow one another in the cache, each its own size.
# h: f32 [d], the residual stream; holds the final hidden state on return.
use qmat_chunk, qmat_batch, quantize_q8, rope_half, silu_mul, swiglu_oai, attn_split, attn_split_q8, attn_merge

fn llama_decode(model:ptr, cfg:ptr, cache:ptr, token:i64, pos:i64, h:ptr, eps:f32)->i64
  b0:
    d, nl, nh, nkv, hd, f, vocab, max_ctx, kvf = call load_cfg(cfg)
    n_exp, n_used, gating, act = call load_moe(cfg)
    embd, norm_out, lm, cos_t, sin_t = call model_globals(model)
    w = vl f32
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    # h = embedding row of the token.
    e_off = mul token, d4
    e_row = add embd, e_off
    jmp embed(0:i64)
  embed(ei:i64):
    e_more = lt ei, d
    br e_more, embed_body, setup
  embed_body:
    e_rest = sub d, ei
    ev = ldm e_row[ei]:vx, e_rest:f32
    stm h[ei], ev, e_rest:f32
    ei2 = add ei, w
    jmp embed(ei2)

  setup:
    fe, rd, fs, wscale = call load_ext(cfg, hd)
    qd = mul nh, hd
    kmax0 = max d, qd
    # the dense and shared MLPs' activations (one at a time), and any projection's input
    fw = max f, fs
    kmax1 = max kmax0, fw
    kmax = max kmax1, fe
    xn = alloc d4
    qd4 = mul qd, 4:i64
    qbuf = alloc qd4
    xq = alloc kmax
    nbmax = udiv kmax, 32:i64
    nb16 = mul nbmax, 16:i64
    dx = alloc nb16
    aq = alloc fw
    nbf = udiv fw, 32:i64
    nbf16 = mul nbf, 16:i64
    adx = alloc nbf16
    moe_sz = call moe_scratch(n_exp, n_used, fe)
    moe_buf = alloc moe_sz
    half = udiv rd, 2:i64
    rope_row = mul half, 4:i64
    rope_off = mul pos, rope_row
    cos_r = add cos_t, rope_off
    sin_r = add sin_t, rope_off
    rb = call kv_rb(hd, kvf)
    kv_row = mul nkv, rb
    heads_all0 = mul nkv, 2:i64
    heads_all = add nh, heads_all0
    dchunks = udiv d, 64:i64
    fchunks = udiv f, 64:i64
    schunks = udiv fs, 64:i64
    # attention: splits of 256 positions, a record per query head and split (attn_split),
    # and one for its sink
    npos = add pos, 1:i64
    npos255 = add npos, 255:i64
    splits = udiv npos255, 256:i64
    splits1 = add splits, 1:i64
    hd2 = add hd, 2:i64
    rec = mul hd2, 4:i64
    part0 = mul nh, splits1
    part_sz = mul part0, rec
    part = alloc part_sz
    scale = call attn_scale(hd)
    jmp layers(0:i64, 0:i64)

  layers(l:i64, kc_off:i64):
    l_more = lt l, nl
    br l_more, layer_body, final
  layer_body:
    attn_norm, m_qkv, m_o, ffn_norm, m_gu, m_dn, q_norm, k_norm, router, experts, qkv_b, o_b, router_b, sinks, win = call layer_weights(model, l)
    m_sgu, m_sdn, sel_b = call layer_shared(model, l)
    # the layer's K and V planes: ctx_l positions per KV head (a ring for a window, kv_ring)
    ctx_l, ring = call kv_ring(win, max_ctx)
    kv_plane0 = mul ctx_l, kv_row
    kc = add cache, kc_off
    vc = add kc, kv_plane0
    kv_layer = mul kv_plane0, 2:i64
    kc_next = add kc_off, kv_layer
    call norm_quant(h, attn_norm, xn, xq, dx, d, eps)
    par heads_all, qkv_head(m_qkv, xq, dx, qbuf, kc, vc, d, nh, nkv, hd, pos, ctx_l, kvf, cos_r, sin_r, q_norm, k_norm, eps, qkv_b, ring, rd)
    # the splits of the layer's window (all positions without one)
    lo, s_lo, nsp = call attn_window(npos, win)
    a_tasks = mul nkv, nsp
    par a_tasks, attn_task(qbuf, kc, vc, part, nh, nkv, hd, npos, ctx_l, kvf, nsp, scale, lo, s_lo, ring)
    par nh, attn_out(part, xq, dx, hd, nsp, sinks)
    par dchunks, proj_add(m_o, xq, dx, h, qd, o_b)
    call norm_quant(h, ffn_norm, xn, xq, dx, d, eps)
    is_moe = ne router, 0:ptr
    br is_moe, moe_mlp, dense_mlp
  moe_mlp:
    call moe_ffn(h, xq, dx, router, experts, d, n_exp, n_used, fe, gating, moe_buf, router_b, act, sel_b, wscale)
    # a shared expert: a dense MLP of width fs on the same input, added after the routed ones
    has_shared = ne m_sgu, 0:ptr
    br has_shared, shared_mlp, layer_next
  shared_mlp:
    par schunks, gate_up(m_sgu, xq, dx, aq, adx, d, 0:ptr, act)
    par dchunks, proj_add(m_sdn, aq, adx, h, fs, 0:ptr)
    jmp layer_next
  dense_mlp:
    par fchunks, gate_up(m_gu, xq, dx, aq, adx, d, 0:ptr, act)
    par dchunks, proj_add(m_dn, aq, adx, h, f, 0:ptr)
    jmp layer_next
  layer_next:
    l2 = add l, 1:i64
    jmp layers(l2, kc_next)

  final:
    call norm_quant(h, norm_out, xn, xq, dx, d, eps)
    next = call lm_argmax(lm, xq, dx, d, vocab)
    free moe_buf
    free part
    free adx
    free aq
    free dx
    free xq
    free qbuf
    free xn
    ret next

# Greedy next token: the LM head on the quantized final hidden state (xq, dx) with a fused
# argmax (lm_chunk); the first index wins ties.
fn lm_argmax(lm:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, d:i64, vocab:i64)->i64
  b0:
    vchunks = udiv vocab, 64:i64
    vb4 = mul vchunks, 4:i64
    best = alloc vb4
    vb8 = mul vchunks, 8:i64
    best_idx = alloc vb8
    par vchunks, lm_chunk(lm, xq, dx, best, best_idx, d)
    b_first = ld best:f32
    i_first = ld best_idx:i64
    jmp pick(1:i64, b_first, i_first)
  pick(pc:i64, pv:f32, pi:i64):
    pc_more = lt pc, vchunks
    br pc_more, pick_body, done
  pick_body:
    cv = ld best[pc]:f32
    ci = ld best_idx[pc]:i64
    better = gt cv, pv
    pv2 = select better, cv, pv
    pi2 = select better, ci, pi
    pc2 = add pc, 1:i64
    jmp pick(pc2, pv2, pi2)
  done:
    free best_idx
    free best
    ret pi

# xn = RMSNorm(h) * w, then xq/dx = Q8 quantization of xn.
fn norm_quant(h:ptr, wt:ptr, xn:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, d:i64, eps:f32)
  b0:
    z = cst 0.0:f32
    zero = splat z:vx
    w = vl f32
    jmp sum(0:i64, zero)
  sum(i:i64, acc:vx):
    more = lt i, d
    br more, sum_body, scale
  sum_body:
    rest = sub d, i
    hv = ldm h[i]:vx, rest:f32
    acc2 = vfma hv, hv, acc:f32
    i2 = add i, w
    jmp sum(i2, acc2)
  scale:
    ss = vsum acc:f32
    nf = itof d:f32
    mean = div ss, nf
    mean_eps = add mean, eps
    rms = sqrt mean_eps
    inv = div 1.0:f32, rms
    vinv = splat inv:vx
    jmp norm(0:i64)
  norm(j:i64):
    more_j = lt j, d
    br more_j, norm_body, quant
  norm_body:
    rest_j = sub d, j
    hv_j = ldm h[j]:vx, rest_j:f32
    wv = ldm wt[j]:vx, rest_j:f32
    hs = vmul hv_j, vinv:f32
    y = vmul hs, wv:f32
    stm xn[j], y, rest_j:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp norm(j2)
  quant:
    call quantize_q8(xn, xq, dx, d)
    ret

# Q, K or V head t: 64-row chunks of the QKV projection plus the head's rows of the bias when
# the layer has one, then for q and k the head's RMSNorm when the layer has one (qk_norm) and
# RoPE of its first rd values (GLM-4.5 rotates half of each head). A q head lands in the q buffer; a K or V head in
# a staging row, rounded to bf16 into this position's slot of its KV-cache row after RoPE.
fn qkv_head(t:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, qbuf:ptr, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, d:i64, nh:i64, nkv:i64, hd:i64, pos:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64, cos_r:ptr, sin_r:ptr, q_norm:ptr, k_norm:ptr, eps:f32, bias:ptr, ring:i64, rd:i64)
  b0:
    hd4 = mul hd, 4:i64
    is_q = lt t, nh
    nhk = add nh, nkv
    is_k = lt t, nhk
    q_off = mul t, hd4
    q_dst = add qbuf, q_off
    stage = alloc hd4
    dst = select is_q, q_dst, stage
    per_head = udiv hd, 64:i64
    c0 = mul t, per_head
    jmp chunks(0:i64)
  chunks(i:i64):
    i_more = lt i, per_head
    br i_more, chunk_body, epilogue
  chunk_body:
    c = add c0, i
    o = mul i, 256:i64
    out = add dst, o
    call qmat_chunk(c, mat, xq, dx, out, d)
    i2 = add i, 1:i64
    jmp chunks(i2)
  epilogue:
    b_off = mul t, hd
    call add_rows(dst, bias, b_off, hd)
    br is_k, rotate, store
  rotate:
    call qk_norm(dst, is_q, q_norm, k_norm, hd, eps)
    call rope_half(dst, rd, cos_r, sin_r)
    jmp store
  store:
    br is_q, done, to_cache
  to_cache:
    call kv_put(stage, t, kc, vc, nh, nkv, hd, pos, ctx_l, kvf, ring, is_k)
    jmp done
  done:
    free stage
    ret

# Qwen3's RMSNorm of one q (is_q) or k head of hd values in place, x * w / rms(x) with the
# layer's q_norm or k_norm weights; nothing when the layer has none (a zero pointer). The
# sum of squares runs as norm_quant's does.
fn qk_norm(x:ptr, is_q:i32, q_norm:ptr, k_norm:ptr, hd:i64, eps:f32)
  b0:
    wt = select is_q, q_norm, k_norm
    none = eq wt, 0:ptr
    z = cst 0.0:f32
    zero = splat z:vx
    w = vl f32
    br none, done, sum(0:i64, zero)
  sum(i:i64, acc:vx):
    more = lt i, hd
    br more, sum_body, scale
  sum_body:
    rest = sub hd, i
    xv = ldm x[i]:vx, rest:f32
    acc2 = vfma xv, xv, acc:f32
    i2 = add i, w
    jmp sum(i2, acc2)
  scale:
    ss = vsum acc:f32
    nf = itof hd:f32
    mean = div ss, nf
    mean_eps = add mean, eps
    rms = sqrt mean_eps
    inv = div 1.0:f32, rms
    vinv = splat inv:vx
    jmp norm(0:i64)
  norm(j:i64):
    more_j = lt j, hd
    br more_j, norm_body, done
  norm_body:
    rest_j = sub hd, j
    xv_j = ldm x[j]:vx, rest_j:f32
    wv = ldm wt[j]:vx, rest_j:f32
    xs = vmul xv_j, vinv:f32
    y = vmul xs, wv:f32
    stm x[j], y, rest_j:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp norm(j2)
  done:
    ret

# A mixture-of-experts MLP for one token (Qwen3-MoE's, gpt-oss's), from its quantized normed
# input xq/dx into its residual stream h: the router picks the n_used experts with the
# largest softmax probabilities (moe_route), each expert's gate/up rows, their bias and the
# activation run in one `par` (64 rows of one expert per task, gate_up), and the down
# projections and their bias in another (moe_down), which adds the experts' outputs, each
# times its weight, in the order they were picked. scratch holds moe_scratch's bytes
# (allocated once per call of llama_decode or llama_prefill).
fn moe_ffn(h:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, router:ptr, experts:ptr, d:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64, gating:i64, scratch:ptr, router_b:ptr, act:i64, sel_b:ptr, wscale:f32)
  b0:
    logits, sel, wts, aq, adx = call moe_buffers(scratch, n_exp, n_used, fe)
    call moe_route(router, xq, dx, logits, sel, wts, d, n_exp, n_used, gating, router_b, sel_b, wscale)
    fchunks = udiv fe, 64:i64
    tasks = mul n_used, fchunks
    par tasks, moe_gate_up(experts, sel, xq, dx, aq, adx, d, fe, act)
    dchunks = udiv d, 64:i64
    par dchunks, moe_down(experts, sel, wts, aq, adx, h, fe, n_used)
    ret

# Bytes of moe_ffn's scratch buffer: the router's logits and the scores it picks by (n_exp
# rounded up to 64 each, moe_route), the
# picked experts and their weights, and each picked expert's int8 activations and block
# records (at least 64, so a dense model allocates something).
inline fn moe_scratch(n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64)->i64
  b0:
    ne63 = add n_exp, 63:i64
    ne_pad = and ne63, -64:i64
    lg = mul ne_pad, 8:i64
    sw = mul n_used, 12:i64
    a = mul n_used, fe
    a2 = mul a, 3:i64
    ad = udiv a2, 2:i64
    t0 = add lg, sw
    t1 = add t0, ad
    t = add t1, 64:i64
    ret t

# moe_ffn's buffers in its scratch: logits, picked experts (i64), their weights (f32), and
# the experts' int8 activations then block records.
inline fn moe_buffers(scratch:ptr, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64)->(ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr)
  b0:
    ne63 = add n_exp, 63:i64
    ne_pad = and ne63, -64:i64
    lg = mul ne_pad, 8:i64
    sel = add scratch, lg
    s8 = mul n_used, 8:i64
    wts = add sel, s8
    s4 = mul n_used, 4:i64
    aq = add wts, s4
    a = mul n_used, fe
    adx = add aq, a
    ret scratch, sel, wts, aq, adx

# The router: logits = router x (plus its bias, when the layer has one), then the n_used
# experts with the largest scores (the first on ties), each one's weight into wts and its
# index into sel, in that order. By `gating`, with softmax numerators e_i = exp(logit_i - max)
# as the scores: 0 the weight is the softmax probability e_i / sum(e); 1 that, then divided
# by the picked ones' sum (at least 2^-14, as llama.cpp clamps it; Qwen3-MoE); 2 the softmax
# of the picked logits, e_i over the picked numerators' sum (gpt-oss). With sigmoid
# probabilities p_i = 1 / (1 + exp(-logit_i)) (DeepSeek-V3's, GLM-4.5's, dots.llm1's): the
# experts are picked by p_i plus the layer's selection bias (sel_b, when not 0) and weighted
# by p_i, 3 divided by the picked ones' sum (clamped as in 1), 4 not. Every weight is then
# multiplied by wscale (the routed experts' scale, 1 for most models). logits holds 2 rows of
# n_exp rounded up to 64: the logits (then the scores or probabilities), and the sigmoid's
# selection scores.
fn moe_route(router:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, logits:ptr, sel:ptr, wts:ptr, d:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, gating:i64, router_b:ptr, sel_b:ptr, wscale:f32)
  b0:
    # The router has n_exp rows rounded up to 64 (zero rows past n_exp), whose logits only
    # fill the buffer: the softmax and the choice read the first n_exp.
    ne63 = add n_exp, 63:i64
    chunks = udiv ne63, 64:i64
    ne_pad = mul chunks, 64:i64
    sv_off = mul ne_pad, 4:i64
    selv = add logits, sv_off
    low = cst -340282346638528859811704183484516925440.0:f32
    is_sig = uge gating, 3:i64
    jmp rows(0:i64)
  rows(c:i64):
    c_more = lt c, chunks
    br c_more, rows_body, biased
  rows_body:
    o = mul c, 256:i64
    out = add logits, o
    call qmat_chunk(c, router, xq, dx, out, d)
    c2 = add c, 1:i64
    jmp rows(c2)
  biased:
    call add_rows(logits, router_b, 0:i64, n_exp)
    br is_sig, sigmoid, max_loop(0:i64, -3.4e38:f32)
  # p = 1 / (1 + exp(-logit)) in place, and the selection scores p + sel_b.
  sigmoid:
    call sigmoid_scores(logits, selv, sel_b, n_exp)
    jmp pick_start(selv, 1.0:f32)
  max_loop(i:i64, m:f32):
    i_more = lt i, n_exp
    br i_more, max_body, softmax
  max_body:
    li = ld logits[i]:f32
    m2 = max m, li
    i2 = add i, 1:i64
    jmp max_loop(i2, m2)
  softmax:
    total = call exp_shift(logits, n_exp, m)
    over_picked = eq gating, 2:i64
    denom0 = select over_picked, 1.0:f32, total
    jmp pick_start(logits, denom0)
  # Scores in sb (the numerators themselves, or the sigmoid's selection scores); a weight is
  # the picked expert's numerator or probability (logits[best]) over denom.
  pick_start(sb:ptr, denom:f32):
    jmp pick(0:i64, 0.0:f32)
  pick(s:i64, wsum:f32):
    s_more = lt s, n_used
    br s_more, scan(0:i64, 0:i64, low), renorm
  scan(j:i64, best:i64, bv:f32):
    j_more = lt j, n_exp
    br j_more, scan_body, picked
  scan_body:
    v = ld sb[j]:f32
    better = gt v, bv
    best2 = select better, j, best
    bv2 = select better, v, bv
    j2 = add j, 1:i64
    jmp scan(j2, best2, bv2)
  picked:
    st sel[s], best
    num = ld logits[best]:f32
    wt = div num, denom
    st wts[s], wt
    # Taken: below every score.
    st sb[best], low
    wsum2 = add wsum, wt
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp pick(s2, wsum2)
  renorm:
    g0 = eq gating, 0:i64
    g4 = eq gating, 4:i64
    no_norm = or g0, g4
    br no_norm, scale_loop(0:i64), norm_start
  norm_start:
    clamped = max wsum, 0.00006103515625:f32
    jmp norm_loop(0:i64)
  norm_loop(r:i64):
    r_more = lt r, n_used
    br r_more, norm_body, scale_loop(0:i64)
  norm_body:
    wr = ld wts[r]:f32
    wn = div wr, clamped
    st wts[r], wn
    r2 = add r, 1:i64
    jmp norm_loop(r2)
  scale_loop(q:i64):
    q_more = lt q, n_used
    br q_more, scale_body, done
  scale_body:
    wq = ld wts[q]:f32
    ws = mul wq, wscale
    st wts[q], ws
    q2 = add q, 1:i64
    jmp scale_loop(q2)
  done:
    ret

# Sigmoid probabilities 1 / (1 + exp(-x)) of the first n logits in place, and the selection
# scores p + b into sv (b the layer's selection bias, or nothing when 0).
fn sigmoid_scores(x:ptr, sv:ptr, b:ptr, n:i64)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    v_one = splat 1.0:f32:vx
    v_zero = splat 0.0:f32:vx
    jmp loop(0:i64)
  loop(i:i64):
    more = lt i, n
    br more, body, bias
  body:
    rest = sub n, i
    xv = ldm x[i]:vx, rest:f32
    nx = vsub v_zero, xv:f32
    e = vexp nx:f32
    den = vadd e, v_one:f32
    p = vdiv v_one, den:f32
    stm x[i], p, rest:f32
    stm sv[i], p, rest:f32
    i2 = add i, w
    jmp loop(i2)
  bias:
    call add_rows(sv, b, 0:i64, n)
    ret

# Task t of an expert MLP: rows 64c..64c+63 of picked expert s (t = s * fe/64 + c), into
# that expert's slot of the down projections' int8 input (fe values per slot).
fn moe_gate_up(t:i64, experts:ptr, sel:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, aq:ptr, adx:ptr, d:i64, fe:i64, act:i64)
  b0:
    fchunks = udiv fe, 64:i64
    s = udiv t, fchunks
    c = urem t, fchunks
    e = ld sel[s]:i64
    e4 = mul e, 4:i64
    mat = ld experts[e4]:ptr
    e42 = add e4, 2:i64
    bias = ld experts[e42]:ptr
    q_off = mul s, fe
    aq_s = add aq, q_off
    d_off = udiv q_off, 2:i64
    adx_s = add adx, d_off
    call gate_up(c, mat, xq, dx, aq_s, adx_s, d, bias, act)
    ret

# Rows 64c..64c+63 of the residual stream += the sum over the picked experts, in the order
# they were picked, of each one's weight times its down projection (plus its bias).
fn moe_down(c:i64, experts:ptr, sel:ptr, wts:ptr, aq:ptr, adx:ptr, h:ptr, fe:i64, n_used:i64)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    tmp = stack 256
    acc = stack 256
    zero = splat 0.0:f32:vx
    jmp clear(0:i64)
  clear(j:i64):
    j_more = lt j, 64:i64
    br j_more, clear_body, slots(0:i64)
  clear_body:
    j_rest = sub 64:i64, j
    stm acc[j], zero, j_rest:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp clear(j2)
  slots(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, n_used
    br s_more, slot_body, add_h(0:i64)
  slot_body:
    e = ld sel[s]:i64
    e4 = mul e, 4:i64
    e41 = add e4, 1:i64
    mat = ld experts[e41]:ptr
    e43 = add e4, 3:i64
    bias = ld experts[e43]:ptr
    q_off = mul s, fe
    aq_s = add aq, q_off
    d_off = udiv q_off, 2:i64
    adx_s = add adx, d_off
    call qmat_chunk(c, mat, aq_s, adx_s, tmp, fe)
    b_off = mul c, 64:i64
    call add_rows(tmp, bias, b_off, 64:i64)
    ws = ld wts[s]:f32
    vw = splat ws:vx
    jmp mix(0:i64)
  mix(k:i64):
    k_more = lt k, 64:i64
    br k_more, mix_body, slot_next
  mix_body:
    k_rest = sub 64:i64, k
    tv = ldm tmp[k]:vx, k_rest:f32
    av = ldm acc[k]:vx, k_rest:f32
    nv = vfma tv, vw, av:f32
    stm acc[k], nv, k_rest:f32
    k2 = add k, w
    jmp mix(k2)
  slot_next:
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp slots(s2)
  add_h(a:i64):
    a_more = lt a, 64:i64
    br a_more, add_body, done
  add_body:
    a_rest = sub 64:i64, a
    h_off = mul c, 256:i64
    hc = add h, h_off
    acv = ldm acc[a]:vx, a_rest:f32
    hv = ldm hc[a]:vx, a_rest:f32
    sum = vadd hv, acv:f32
    stm hc[a], sum, a_rest:f32
    a2 = add a, w
    jmp add_h(a2)
  done:
    ret

# K (is_k) or V of position p for KV head t (t >= nh), src[0 .. hd] after RoPE, into the
# layer's cache (kv_store at kv_slot's place): at slot p, or in a ring of `ring` slots at p
# mod ring and again at p mod ring + ring (kv_ring).
fn kv_put(src:ptr, t:i64, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, nh:i64, nkv:i64, hd:i64, p:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64, ring:i64, is_k:i32)
  b0:
    slot = call ring_slot(p, ring)
    tile, col = call kv_slot(t, kc, vc, nh, nkv, hd, slot, ctx_l, kvf)
    call kv_store(src, tile, col, hd, is_k, kvf)
    has_ring = ne ring, 0:i64
    br has_ring, mirror, done
  mirror:
    slot2 = add slot, ring
    tile2, col2 = call kv_slot(t, kc, vc, nh, nkv, hd, slot2, ctx_l, kvf)
    call kv_store(src, tile2, col2, hd, is_k, kvf)
    ret
  done:
    ret

# Where K or V head t (t >= nh; a q head gets an unused address) stores slot p: the tile of
# slots p - p mod 32 .. in its plane (head * ctx_l + p - p mod 32 slots of kv_rb bytes in),
# and p mod 32, the slot's column in it.
fn kv_slot(t:i64, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, nh:i64, nkv:i64, hd:i64, p:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64)->(ptr, i64)
  b0:
    nhk = add nh, nkv
    is_k = lt t, nhk
    tk = sub t, nh
    tv = sub t, nhk
    kvh = select is_k, tk, tv
    r0 = mul kvh, ctx_l
    col = and p, 31:i64
    p0 = sub p, col
    r1 = add r0, p0
    rb = call kv_rb(hd, kvf)
    off = mul r1, rb
    base = select is_k, kc, vc
    tile = add base, off
    ret tile, col

# K (is_k) or V of one position, src[0 .. hd] after RoPE, into column col of its cache tile:
# rounded to bf16, K's value j at tile + 64 j + 2 col (a [hd x 32] tile) and V's row at
# tile + 2 hd col; or for an int8 cache (kvf 1) as attn_split_q8 reads them (to_q8_kv).
fn kv_store(src:ptr, tile:ptr, col:i64, hd:i64, is_k:i32, kvf:i64)
  b0:
    is_q8 = eq kvf, 1:i64
    br is_q8, q8, bf16
  q8:
    call to_q8_kv(src, tile, col, hd, is_k)
    ret
  bf16:
    br is_k, k, v
  k:
    col2 = shl col, 1:i64
    kt = add tile, col2
    call to_bf16_kt(src, kt, hd)
    ret
  v:
    row0 = mul col, hd
    row1 = shl row0, 1:i64
    vr = add tile, row1
    call to_bf16(src, vr, hd)
    ret

# K or V of one position into column col of an int8 cache tile (see attn_split_q8): src[0 ..
# hd] over d = max |x| / 127, rounded to int8 (half away from zero, as quantize_q8 does); K's
# values plus 128, byte q of group g at tile + 128 g + 4 col + q, V's at tile + hd col; d at
# tile + 32 hd + 4 col.
fn to_q8_kv(src:ptr, tile:ptr, col:i64, hd:i64, is_k:i32)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    zf = cst 0.0:f32
    v_zero = splat zf:vx
    row = alloc hd
    jmp amax(0:i64, v_zero)
  amax(t:i64, a:vx):
    t_more = lt t, hd
    br t_more, amax_body, scale
  amax_body:
    rest = sub hd, t
    v = ldm src[t]:vx, rest:f32
    av = vabs v:f32
    a2 = vmax a, av:f32
    t2 = add t, w
    jmp amax(t2, a2)
  scale:
    am = vmaxr a:f32
    d = div am, 127.0:f32
    pos = gt d, zf
    inv = div 1.0:f32, d
    id = select pos, inv, zf
    v_id = splat id:vx
    sc0 = shl hd, 5:i64
    col4 = shl col, 2:i64
    sc1 = add sc0, col4
    sp = add tile, sc1
    st sp, d
    jmp quant(0:i64)
  quant(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, hd
    br s_more, quant_body, place
  quant_body:
    rest_q = sub hd, s
    xv = ldm src[s]:vx, rest_q:f32
    sv = vmul xv, v_id:f32
    rv = vround sv:f32
    qi = vftoi rv:i32
    q16 = vnarrow qi, qi:i16
    q8 = vnarrow q16, q16:i8
    cnt = min rest_q, w
    stm row[s:i8], q8, cnt:i8
    s2 = add s, w
    jmp quant(s2)
  place:
    br is_k, k(0:i64), v_row
  k(g:i64):
    g_more = lt g, hd
    br g_more, k_body, done
  k_body:
    gi = ushr g, 2:i64
    x = ld row[gi]:i32
    xu = xor x, -2139062144:i32
    go = shl g, 5:i64
    ko = add go, col4
    kp = add tile, ko
    st kp, xu
    g2 = add g, 4:i64
    jmp k(g2)
  v_row:
    vo = mul col, hd
    vp = add tile, vo
    call copy_f32(row, vp, hd)
    jmp done
  done:
    free row
    ret

# K of one position into its cache tile: src[0 .. n] rounded to bf16 as to_bf16 does, value
# j at dst + 64 j (column of a [n x 32] tile).
fn to_bf16_kt(src:ptr, dst:ptr, n:i64)
  b0:
    n2 = mul n, 2:i64
    row = alloc n2
    call to_bf16(src, row, n)
    jmp loop(0:i64)
  loop(j:i64):
    more = lt j, n
    br more, body, done
  body:
    v = ld row[j]:i16
    o = mul j, 64:i64
    dj = add dst, o
    st dj, v
    j2 = add j, 1:i64
    jmp loop(j2)
  done:
    free row
    ret

# dst[0 .. n] = src[0 .. n] rounded to bf16 (nearest even).
fn to_bf16(src:ptr, dst:ptr, n:i64)
  b0:
    w16 = vl bf16
    w32 = vl f32
    jmp loop(0:i64)
  loop(j:i64):
    more = lt j, n
    br more, body, done
  body:
    rest = sub n, j
    rest_hi0 = sub rest, w32
    rest_hi = max rest_hi0, 0:i64
    j_hi = add j, w32
    lo = ldm src[j]:vx, rest:f32
    hi = ldm src[j_hi]:vx, rest_hi:f32
    v = vnarrow lo, hi:bf16
    stm dst[j], v, rest:bf16
    j2 = add j, w16
    jmp loop(j2)
  done:
    ret

# 1 / sqrt(hd), the attention scores' scale.
fn attn_scale(hd:i64)->f32
  b0:
    hdf = itof hd:f32
    sq = sqrt hdf
    scale = div 1.0:f32, sq
    ret scale

# The window of a layer whose queries see the last win positions (0: all of them) for a query
# at npos - 1: its first position lo, its first split s_lo (of 256 positions) and its number
# of splits.
inline fn attn_window(npos:i64, win:i64)->(i64, i64, i64)
  b0:
    none = eq win, 0:i64
    lo0 = sub npos, win
    lo1 = max lo0, 0:i64
    lo = select none, 0:i64, lo1
    s_lo = udiv lo, 256:i64
    n255 = add npos, 255:i64
    splits = udiv n255, 256:i64
    nsp = sub splits, s_lo
    ret lo, s_lo, nsp

# Split s_lo + i of KV head g (task = g * nsp + i): positions max(256 s, lo) .. of the first
# npos, for the group's query heads; records in `part`, head h's i-th at (h * (nsp + 1) + i)
# * (hd + 2) f32, the last of a head's nsp + 1 for its sink (attn_out).
fn attn_task(task:i64, qbuf:ptr, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, part:ptr, nh:i64, nkv:i64, hd:i64, npos:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64, nsp:i64, scale:f32, lo:i64, s_lo:i64, ring:i64)
  b0:
    g = udiv task, nsp
    i = urem task, nsp
    s = add s_lo, i
    group = udiv nh, nkv
    h0 = mul g, group
    hd4 = mul hd, 4:i64
    q_off = mul h0, hd4
    qg = add qbuf, q_off
    hd2 = add hd, 2:i64
    rec = mul hd2, 4:i64
    nsp1 = add nsp, 1:i64
    head_b = mul nsp1, rec
    p0 = mul h0, head_b
    p1 = mul i, rec
    p2 = add p0, p1
    pg = add part, p2
    call attn_part(g, s, qg, kc, vc, pg, group, hd, npos, ctx_l, kvf, scale, head_b, lo, ring)
    ret

# One split of attention (attn_split, or attn_split_q8 for an int8 cache) for KV head g:
# positions max(256 s, lo) .. 256 s + 256 of the first npos (lo < npos), query heads at qg,
# records from pg (head_b bytes per head). The cache is read from the tile of 32 positions
# that holds the first one; attn_split leaves the positions before it out. In a ring (kv_ring)
# the tile's slot is its position mod ring: the read spans at most ring slots, which the
# ring's second copy keeps contiguous.
fn attn_part(g:i64, s:i64, qg:ptr, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, pg:ptr, group:i64, hd:i64, npos:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64, scale:f32, head_b:i64, lo:i64, ring:i64)
  b0:
    t0 = mul s, 256:i64
    t_end0 = add t0, 256:i64
    t1 = min t_end0, npos
    ta = max t0, lo
    skip = and ta, 31:i64
    tb = sub ta, skip
    nt = sub t1, tb
    g_rows = mul g, ctx_l
    tb_slot = call ring_slot(tb, ring)
    first = add g_rows, tb_slot
    rb = call kv_rb(hd, kvf)
    kv_off = mul first, rb
    kb = add kc, kv_off
    vb = add vc, kv_off
    is_q8 = eq kvf, 1:i64
    br is_q8, q8, bf16
  bf16:
    call attn_split(qg, kb, vb, pg, group, hd, nt, skip, scale, head_b)
    ret
  q8:
    call attn_split_q8(qg, kb, vb, pg, group, hd, nt, skip, scale, head_b)
    ret

# Query head hq: merges its nsp splits and its sink (merge_quant) and writes the result
# Q8-quantized into xq/dx at the head's offset, the O projection's input.
fn attn_out(hq:i64, part:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, hd:i64, nsp:i64, sinks:ptr)
  b0:
    hd2 = add hd, 2:i64
    rec = mul hd2, 4:i64
    nsp1 = add nsp, 1:i64
    head_b = mul nsp1, rec
    hp_off = mul hq, head_b
    hp = add part, hp_off
    call merge_quant(hp, nsp, hd, hq, xq, dx, sinks)
    ret

# attn_merge of a query head's splits (records from hp), quantized into xq/dx at head hq.
# With attention sinks (gpt-oss: a logit per query head that takes part in the softmax but
# has no value), the head's sink is one more record after the splits, max sinks[hq], sum 1
# and outputs 0, so the merge adds exp(sink - m) to the softmax's denominator alone.
fn merge_quant(hp:ptr, splits:i64, hd:i64, hq:i64, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, sinks:ptr)
  b0:
    hd4 = mul hd, 4:i64
    out = alloc hd4
    hd2 = add hd, 2:i64
    rec = mul hd2, 4:i64
    w = vl f32
    zero = splat 0.0:f32:vx
    has_sink = ne sinks, 0:ptr
    br has_sink, sink, merge(splits)
  sink:
    sk_off = mul splits, rec
    sk = add hp, sk_off
    sv = ld sinks[hq]:f32
    st sk, sv
    st sk[1], 1.0:f32
    sk_o = add sk, 8:i64
    jmp sink_zero(0:i64)
  sink_zero(z:i64):
    z_more = lt z, hd
    br z_more, sink_zero_body, sink_done
  sink_zero_body:
    z_rest = sub hd, z
    stm sk_o[z], zero, z_rest:f32
    z2 = add z, w
    jmp sink_zero(z2)
  sink_done:
    with_sink = add splits, 1:i64
    jmp merge(with_sink)
  merge(count:i64):
    call attn_merge(hp, count, rec, hd, out)
    xq_off = mul hq, hd
    xq_h = add xq, xq_off
    blocks = udiv hd, 32:i64
    dx_off0 = mul hq, blocks
    dx_off = mul dx_off0, 16:i64
    dx_h = add dx, dx_off
    call quantize_q8(out, xq_h, dx_h, hd)
    free out
    ret

# h[64c .. 64c + 64] += (W x + b)[64c .. 64c + 64]: a projection fused with the residual add
# (b the bias, when not 0).
fn proj_add(c:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, h:ptr, k:i64, bias:ptr)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    tmp = stack 256
    call qmat_chunk(c, mat, xq, dx, tmp, k)
    b_off = mul c, 64:i64
    call add_rows(tmp, bias, b_off, 64:i64)
    h_off = mul c, 256:i64
    hc = add h, h_off
    jmp add_loop(0:i64)
  add_loop(j:i64):
    more = lt j, 64:i64
    br more, add_body, done
  add_body:
    rest = sub 64:i64, j
    tv = ldm tmp[j]:vx, rest:f32
    hv = ldm hc[j]:vx, rest:f32
    s = vadd hv, tv:f32
    stm hc[j], s, rest:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp add_loop(j2)
  done:
    ret

# MLP rows 64c..64c+63: gate and up chunks plus their rows of the bias (laid out as the
# matrix's rows, when not 0), the activation (glu), then Q8 quantization for the down
# projection (two 32-blocks per task).
fn gate_up(c:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, aq:ptr, adx:ptr, k:i64, bias:ptr, act:i64)
  b0:
    g = stack 256
    u = stack 256
    a = stack 256
    cg = mul c, 2:i64
    cu = add cg, 1:i64
    call qmat_chunk(cg, mat, xq, dx, g, k)
    call qmat_chunk(cu, mat, xq, dx, u, k)
    gb = mul cg, 64:i64
    call add_rows(g, bias, gb, 64:i64)
    ub = mul cu, 64:i64
    call add_rows(u, bias, ub, 64:i64)
    call glu(g, u, a, 64:i64, act)
    q_off = mul c, 64:i64
    aq_c = add aq, q_off
    d_off = mul c, 32:i64
    adx_c = add adx, d_off
    call quantize_q8(a, aq_c, adx_c, 64:i64)
    ret

# LM head rows 64c..64c+63, keeping only the best logit (first on ties) and its token.
fn lm_chunk(c:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, best:ptr, best_idx:ptr, k:i64)
  b0:
    tmp = stack 256
    call qmat_chunk(c, mat, xq, dx, tmp, k)
    first = ld tmp:f32
    jmp scan(1:i64, first, 0:i64)
  scan(j:i64, bv:f32, bj:i64):
    more = lt j, 64:i64
    br more, scan_body, done
  scan_body:
    v = ld tmp[j]:f32
    better = gt v, bv
    bv2 = select better, v, bv
    bj2 = select better, j, bj
    j2 = add j, 1:i64
    jmp scan(j2, bv2, bj2)
  done:
    st best[c], bv
    base = mul c, 64:i64
    tok = add base, bj
    st best_idx[c], tok
    ret

# x[0 .. n] += b[off .. off + n], when b is not 0 (a layer's bias).
fn add_rows(x:ptr, b:ptr, off:i64, n:i64)
  b0:
    none = eq b, 0:ptr
    w = vl f32
    b_off = shl off, 2:i64
    bo = add b, b_off
    br none, done, loop(0:i64)
  loop(i:i64):
    more = lt i, n
    br more, body, done
  body:
    rest = sub n, i
    xv = ldm x[i]:vx, rest:f32
    bv = ldm bo[i]:vx, rest:f32
    y = vadd xv, bv:f32
    stm x[i], y, rest:f32
    i2 = add i, w
    jmp loop(i2)
  done:
    ret

# The MLP's activation of n gate and up values into out, by act: 0 SwiGLU (silu_mul), 1
# gpt-oss's clamped SwiGLU (swiglu_oai: alpha 1.702, limit 7).
fn glu(g:ptr, u:ptr, out:ptr, n:i64, act:i64)
  b0:
    oai = eq act, 1:i64
    br oai, clamped, silu
  clamped:
    call swiglu_oai(g, u, out, n, 1.702:f32, 7.0:f32)
    ret
  silu:
    call silu_mul(g, u, out, n)
    ret

# Prefill: n prompt tokens (i64 [n] at `tokens`) at positions pos .. pos + n - 1, with the
# model, cache and h of llama_decode (pos + n <= max_ctx). Returns the greedy token after
# the last one; h holds the last token's final hidden state. Per layer: 2 norm passes over
# the tokens, then `par` regions like llama_decode's, each projection task computing its rows
# for every token (8 tokens per weight load). Attention runs one task per tile of 8 tokens
# and KV head, each token over the cache up to its own position (so tokens never see later
# ones), with the same splits and merges as llama_decode's (attn_tok). A mixture of experts
# runs on batches of up to 256 tokens, each expert's weights read once for the batch's
# tokens that picked it (moe_ffn_n). A model with a ring in its cache (kv_ring) runs the
# prompt in pieces of up to 256 tokens (prefill_part), whose K and V the ring holds next to
# the windows that read them.
fn llama_prefill(model:ptr, cfg:ptr, cache:ptr, tokens:ptr, n:i64, pos:i64, h:ptr, eps:f32)->i64
  b0:
    nl = ld cfg[1]:i64
    ctx0 = ld cfg[7]:i64
    ctx31 = add ctx0, 31:i64
    max_ctx = and ctx31, -32:i64
    jmp scan(0:i64, 0:i64)
  scan(l:i64, rings:i64):
    l_more = lt l, nl
    br l_more, scan_body, split
  scan_body:
    slot0 = mul l, 18:i64
    slot = add slot0, 19:i64
    win = ld model[slot]:i64
    ctx_l_, ring = call kv_ring(win, max_ctx)
    has = ne ring, 0:i64
    has64 = zext has:i64
    rings2 = or rings, has64
    l2 = add l, 1:i64
    jmp scan(l2, rings2)
  split:
    any_ring = ne rings, 0:i64
    piece = select any_ring, 256:i64, n
    jmp parts(0:i64, 0:i64)
  parts(done:i64, last:i64):
    more = lt done, n
    br more, part_body, finish
  part_body:
    left = sub n, done
    m = min left, piece
    t_off = mul done, 8:i64
    toks = add tokens, t_off
    p = add pos, done
    next = call prefill_part(model, cfg, cache, toks, m, p, h, eps)
    done2 = add done, m
    jmp parts(done2, next)
  finish:
    ret last

# llama_prefill on n tokens at once: every layer's passes over all of them.
fn prefill_part(model:ptr, cfg:ptr, cache:ptr, tokens:ptr, n:i64, pos:i64, h:ptr, eps:f32)->i64
  b0:
    d, nl, nh, nkv, hd, f, vocab, max_ctx, kvf = call load_cfg(cfg)
    n_exp, n_used, gating, act = call load_moe(cfg)
    fe, rd, fs, wscale = call load_ext(cfg, hd)
    embd, norm_out, lm, cos_t, sin_t = call model_globals(model)
    w = vl f32
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    # hs: the residual streams of the n tokens, f32 [n x d].
    hs_sz = mul n, d4
    hs = alloc hs_sz
    jmp embed_tok(0:i64)
  embed_tok(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, n
    br s_more, embed_start, setup
  embed_start:
    tok = ld tokens[s]:i64
    e_off = mul tok, d4
    e_row = add embd, e_off
    h_off = mul s, d4
    h_row = add hs, h_off
    jmp embed(0:i64)
  embed(ei:i64):
    e_more = lt ei, d
    br e_more, embed_body, embed_next
  embed_body:
    e_rest = sub d, ei
    ev = ldm e_row[ei]:vx, e_rest:f32
    stm h_row[ei], ev, e_rest:f32
    ei2 = add ei, w
    jmp embed(ei2)
  embed_next:
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp embed_tok(s2)

  setup:
    qd = mul nh, hd
    kmax0 = max d, qd
    # xs: bytes per token in the int8 activation buffers (any projection's input fits).
    xs0 = max kmax0, f
    xs1 = max xs0, fe
    xs = max xs1, fs
    xn = alloc hs_sz
    qd4 = mul qd, 4:i64
    qb_sz = mul n, qd4
    qbuf = alloc qb_sz
    xq_sz = mul n, xs
    xq = alloc xq_sz
    aq = alloc xq_sz
    dx_sz = udiv xq_sz, 2:i64
    dx = alloc dx_sz
    adx = alloc dx_sz
    # mixtures of experts: batches of up to 256 tokens, grouped by expert (moe_ffn_n)
    moe_nb = min n, 256:i64
    moe_sz = call moe_scratch_n(moe_nb, n_exp, n_used, fe, d)
    moe_buf = alloc moe_sz
    rb = call kv_rb(hd, kvf)
    kv_row = mul nkv, rb
    heads_all0 = mul nkv, 2:i64
    heads_all = add nh, heads_all0
    dchunks = udiv d, 64:i64
    fchunks = udiv f, 64:i64
    schunks = udiv fs, 64:i64
    # attention: tiles of 8 tokens per KV head
    tiles0 = add n, 7:i64
    tiles = udiv tiles0, 8:i64
    a_tasks = mul tiles, nkv
    scale = call attn_scale(hd)
    jmp layers(0:i64, 0:i64)

  layers(l:i64, kc_off:i64):
    l_more = lt l, nl
    br l_more, layer_body, final
  layer_body:
    attn_norm, m_qkv, m_o, ffn_norm, m_gu, m_dn, q_norm, k_norm, router, experts, qkv_b, o_b, router_b, sinks, win = call layer_weights(model, l)
    m_sgu, m_sdn, sel_b = call layer_shared(model, l)
    ctx_l, ring = call kv_ring(win, max_ctx)
    kv_plane0 = mul ctx_l, kv_row
    kc = add cache, kc_off
    vc = add kc, kv_plane0
    kv_layer = mul kv_plane0, 2:i64
    kc_next = add kc_off, kv_layer
    par n, norm_tok(hs, attn_norm, xn, xq, dx, d, eps, xs)
    par heads_all, qkv_head_n(m_qkv, xq, dx, qbuf, kc, vc, d, nh, nkv, hd, pos, ctx_l, kvf, cos_t, sin_t, n, xs, q_norm, k_norm, eps, qkv_b, ring, rd)
    par a_tasks, attn_tok(qbuf, kc, vc, xq, dx, nh, nkv, hd, pos, ctx_l, kvf, scale, xs, n, win, sinks, ring)
    par dchunks, proj_add_n(m_o, xq, dx, hs, qd, n, xs, d, o_b)
    par n, norm_tok(hs, ffn_norm, xn, xq, dx, d, eps, xs)
    is_moe = ne router, 0:ptr
    br is_moe, moe_batch(0:i64), dense_mlp
  # The tokens' experts in batches of up to 256 tokens, each expert's weights read once for
  # the batch's tokens that picked it, with llama_decode's results (moe_ffn_n).
  moe_batch(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, n
    br s_more, moe_body, moe_shared
  moe_body:
    left = sub n, s
    nb = min left, moe_nb
    h_off = mul s, d4
    h_s = add hs, h_off
    x_off = mul s, xs
    xq_s = add xq, x_off
    ds = udiv xs, 2:i64
    d_off = mul s, ds
    dx_s = add dx, d_off
    call moe_ffn_n(h_s, xq_s, dx_s, nb, xs, router, experts, d, n_exp, n_used, fe, gating, moe_buf, router_b, act, moe_nb, sel_b, wscale)
    s2 = add s, nb
    jmp moe_batch(s2)
  # a shared expert after the routed ones, as llama_decode adds it
  moe_shared:
    has_shared = ne m_sgu, 0:ptr
    br has_shared, shared_mlp, layer_next
  shared_mlp:
    par schunks, gate_up_n(m_sgu, xq, dx, aq, adx, d, n, xs, 0:ptr, act)
    par dchunks, proj_add_n(m_sdn, aq, adx, hs, fs, n, xs, d, 0:ptr)
    jmp layer_next
  dense_mlp:
    par fchunks, gate_up_n(m_gu, xq, dx, aq, adx, d, n, xs, 0:ptr, act)
    par dchunks, proj_add_n(m_dn, aq, adx, hs, f, n, xs, d, 0:ptr)
    jmp layer_next
  layer_next:
    l2 = add l, 1:i64
    jmp layers(l2, kc_next)

  final:
    last = sub n, 1:i64
    last_off = mul last, d4
    h_last = add hs, last_off
    jmp copy(0:i64)
  copy(ci:i64):
    c_more = lt ci, d
    br c_more, copy_body, head
  copy_body:
    c_rest = sub d, ci
    cv = ldm h_last[ci]:vx, c_rest:f32
    stm h[ci], cv, c_rest:f32
    ci2 = add ci, w
    jmp copy(ci2)
  head:
    call norm_quant(h, norm_out, xn, xq, dx, d, eps)
    next = call lm_argmax(lm, xq, dx, d, vocab)
    free moe_buf
    free adx
    free dx
    free aq
    free xq
    free qbuf
    free xn
    free hs
    ret next

# norm_quant for token s of a prefill: its residual stream row of hs, its xn row, and its
# int8 activations xs bytes apart (block records xs / 2 apart).
fn norm_tok(s:i64, hs:ptr, wt:ptr, xn:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, d:i64, eps:f32, xs:i64)
  b0:
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    r_off = mul s, d4
    h_s = add hs, r_off
    xn_s = add xn, r_off
    q_off = mul s, xs
    xq_s = add xq, q_off
    ds = udiv xs, 2:i64
    d_off = mul s, ds
    dx_s = add dx, d_off
    call norm_quant(h_s, wt, xn_s, xq_s, dx_s, d, eps)
    ret

# qkv_head for n tokens: head t's 64-row chunks for every token (qmat_batch), each token's
# rows written to its q row or a staging row, then the head's bias, norm (qk_norm) and RoPE
# at its position and, for K and V, bf16 into its position's KV-cache slot.
fn qkv_head_n(t:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, qbuf:ptr, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, d:i64, nh:i64, nkv:i64, hd:i64, pos:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64, cos_t:ptr, sin_t:ptr, n:i64, xs:i64, q_norm:ptr, k_norm:ptr, eps:f32, bias:ptr, ring:i64, rd:i64)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    hd4 = mul hd, 4:i64
    qd4 = mul nh, hd4
    is_q = lt t, nh
    nhk = add nh, nkv
    is_k = lt t, nhk
    q_off = mul t, hd4
    stage_sz = mul n, hd4
    stage = alloc stage_sz
    half = udiv rd, 2:i64
    rope_row = mul half, 4:i64
    per_head = udiv hd, 64:i64
    c0 = mul t, per_head
    tmp_sz = mul n, 256:i64
    tmp = alloc tmp_sz
    jmp chunks(0:i64)
  chunks(i:i64):
    i_more = lt i, per_head
    br i_more, chunk_body, rope(0:i64)
  chunk_body:
    c = add c0, i
    call qmat_batch(c, mat, xq, dx, tmp, d, n, xs)
    o = mul i, 256:i64
    jmp scatter(0:i64)
  scatter(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, n
    br s_more, scatter_start, chunk_next
  scatter_start:
    sq = mul s, qd4
    q_dst0 = add qbuf, sq
    q_dst = add q_dst0, q_off
    sg = mul s, hd4
    kv_dst = add stage, sg
    dst0 = select is_q, q_dst, kv_dst
    dst = add dst0, o
    st_off = mul s, 256:i64
    src = add tmp, st_off
    jmp copy(0:i64)
  copy(j:i64):
    j_more = lt j, 64:i64
    br j_more, copy_body, scatter_next
  copy_body:
    j_rest = sub 64:i64, j
    v = ldm src[j]:vx, j_rest:f32
    stm dst[j], v, j_rest:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp copy(j2)
  scatter_next:
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp scatter(s2)
  chunk_next:
    i2 = add i, 1:i64
    jmp chunks(i2)
  rope(r:i64):
    r_more = lt r, n
    br r_more, rope_body, done
  rope_body:
    rq0 = mul r, qd4
    rq1 = add qbuf, rq0
    rq = add rq1, q_off
    rs = mul r, hd4
    rkv = add stage, rs
    x = select is_q, rq, rkv
    rp = add pos, r
    b_off = mul t, hd
    call add_rows(x, bias, b_off, hd)
    br is_k, rotate, store
  rotate:
    rr = mul rp, rope_row
    cos_r = add cos_t, rr
    sin_r = add sin_t, rr
    call qk_norm(x, is_q, q_norm, k_norm, hd, eps)
    call rope_half(x, rd, cos_r, sin_r)
    jmp store
  store:
    br is_q, rope_next, to_cache
  to_cache:
    call kv_put(x, t, kc, vc, nh, nkv, hd, rp, ctx_l, kvf, ring, is_k)
    jmp rope_next
  rope_next:
    r2 = add r, 1:i64
    jmp rope(r2)
  done:
    free stage
    free tmp
    ret

# Attention of a tile of up to 8 tokens s0 .. s0 + tn - 1 for KV head g (task = tile * nkv
# + g), token s over its window of positions up to pos + s (attn_window; all of them
# without one): the same splits (attn_part) and merges with its sink (merge_quant) as
# llama_decode at that position, in a buffer of its own, so its results are llama_decode's
# bit for bit. The splits that every token of the tile sees whole (all 256 positions, inside
# every token's window) run once for all of the tile's query heads, so each K and V vector
# is read from memory once for the tile; attn_split computes each head's row on its own, so
# a row's results do not depend on the heads beside it. Each token's remaining splits run on
# their own. Writes the group's Q8 outputs into each token's activations.
fn attn_tok(task:i64, qbuf:ptr, kc:ptr, vc:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, nh:i64, nkv:i64, hd:i64, pos:i64, ctx_l:i64, kvf:i64, scale:f32, xs:i64, n:i64, win:i64, sinks:ptr, ring:i64)
  b0:
    tile = udiv task, nkv
    g = urem task, nkv
    s0 = mul tile, 8:i64
    left = sub n, s0
    tn = min left, 8:i64
    group = udiv nh, nkv
    h0 = mul g, group
    hd4 = mul hd, 4:i64
    qd4 = mul nh, hd4
    # The first token's first split (the tile's lowest), the last token's window, and the
    # splits every token sees whole: from the last token's window start rounded up to a
    # split, to the first token's last whole split.
    p0 = add pos, s0
    npos0 = add p0, 1:i64
    lo0_, base, nsp0_ = call attn_window(npos0, win)
    npos_last = add p0, tn
    lo_last, slo_last, nsp_last = call attn_window(npos_last, win)
    smax = add slo_last, nsp_last
    lo255 = add lo_last, 255:i64
    sh_lo = udiv lo255, 256:i64
    sh_hi = udiv npos0, 256:i64
    hd2 = add hd, 2:i64
    rec = mul hd2, 4:i64
    # a row's records: splits base .. smax - 1, then room for the last token's sink
    span0 = sub smax, base
    span = add span0, 1:i64
    head_b = mul span, rec
    rows = mul tn, group
    part_sz = mul rows, head_b
    part = alloc part_sz
    # the tile's query heads of KV head g, token by token: rows s * group + r
    gb = mul group, hd4
    qt_sz = mul tn, gb
    qt = alloc qt_sz
    q_h0 = mul h0, hd4
    jmp gather(0:i64)
  gather(gs:i64):
    gs_more = lt gs, tn
    br gs_more, gather_start, shared_splits(sh_lo)
  gather_start:
    gtok = add s0, gs
    gq0 = mul gtok, qd4
    gq1 = add qbuf, gq0
    gsrc = add gq1, q_h0
    gd0 = mul gs, gb
    gdst = add qt, gd0
    call copy_f32(gsrc, gdst, gb)
    gs2 = add gs, 1:i64
    jmp gather(gs2)
  shared_splits(sp:i64):
    sp_more = lt sp, sh_hi
    br sp_more, shared_body, tokens(0:i64)
  shared_body:
    sp_rel = sub sp, base
    sp_off = mul sp_rel, rec
    pg = add part, sp_off
    call attn_part(g, sp, qt, kc, vc, pg, rows, hd, npos0, ctx_l, kvf, scale, head_b, lo_last, ring)
    sp2 = add sp, 1:i64
    jmp shared_splits(sp2)
  # Token by token: its own splits, then the merge of each of its heads.
  tokens(ts:i64):
    ts_more = lt ts, tn
    br ts_more, token_start, done
  token_start:
    s = add s0, ts
    p = add pos, s
    npos = add p, 1:i64
    lo, slo, nsp = call attn_window(npos, win)
    splits = add slo, nsp
    t_rows = mul ts, group
    t_part0 = mul t_rows, head_b
    t_part = add part, t_part0
    t_q0 = mul ts, gb
    t_q = add qt, t_q0
    x_off = mul s, xs
    xq_s = add xq, x_off
    ds = udiv xs, 2:i64
    d_off = mul s, ds
    dx_s = add dx, d_off
    jmp split(slo)
  split(tsp:i64):
    tsp_more = lt tsp, splits
    br tsp_more, split_check, merge(0:i64)
  split_check:
    at_lo = ge tsp, sh_lo
    below_hi = lt tsp, sh_hi
    shared = and at_lo, below_hi
    br shared, split_next, split_body
  split_body:
    tsp_rel = sub tsp, base
    tsp_off = mul tsp_rel, rec
    tpg = add t_part, tsp_off
    call attn_part(g, tsp, t_q, kc, vc, tpg, group, hd, npos, ctx_l, kvf, scale, head_b, lo, ring)
    jmp split_next
  split_next:
    tsp2 = add tsp, 1:i64
    jmp split(tsp2)
  merge(r:i64):
    r_more = lt r, group
    br r_more, merge_body, token_next
  merge_body:
    hp_off = mul r, head_b
    hp0 = add t_part, hp_off
    first_rel = sub slo, base
    first_off = mul first_rel, rec
    hp = add hp0, first_off
    hq = add h0, r
    call merge_quant(hp, nsp, hd, hq, xq_s, dx_s, sinks)
    r2 = add r, 1:i64
    jmp merge(r2)
  token_next:
    ts2 = add ts, 1:i64
    jmp tokens(ts2)
  done:
    free qt
    free part
    ret

# dst[0 .. bytes] = src[0 .. bytes], bytes a multiple of 4.
fn copy_f32(src:ptr, dst:ptr, bytes:i64)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    n = udiv bytes, 4:i64
    jmp loop(0:i64)
  loop(i:i64):
    more = lt i, n
    br more, body, done
  body:
    rest = sub n, i
    v = ldm src[i]:vx, rest:f32
    stm dst[i], v, rest:f32
    i2 = add i, w
    jmp loop(i2)
  done:
    ret

# proj_add for n tokens: rows 64c..64c+63 of every token's residual stream += (W x + b).
fn proj_add_n(c:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, hs:ptr, k:i64, n:i64, xs:i64, d:i64, bias:ptr)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    tmp_sz = mul n, 256:i64
    tmp = alloc tmp_sz
    call qmat_batch(c, mat, xq, dx, tmp, k, n, xs)
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    c_off = mul c, 256:i64
    jmp toks(0:i64)
  toks(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, n
    br s_more, tok_start, done
  tok_start:
    r_off = mul s, d4
    row = add hs, r_off
    hc = add row, c_off
    t_off = mul s, 256:i64
    ts = add tmp, t_off
    b_off = mul c, 64:i64
    call add_rows(ts, bias, b_off, 64:i64)
    jmp add_loop(0:i64)
  add_loop(j:i64):
    more = lt j, 64:i64
    br more, add_body, tok_next
  add_body:
    rest = sub 64:i64, j
    tv = ldm ts[j]:vx, rest:f32
    hv = ldm hc[j]:vx, rest:f32
    sum = vadd hv, tv:f32
    stm hc[j], sum, rest:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp add_loop(j2)
  tok_next:
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp toks(s2)
  done:
    free tmp
    ret

# gate_up for n tokens: MLP rows 64c..64c+63 of every token, their bias and the activation,
# then Q8 quantization into the token's down-projection input.
fn gate_up_n(c:i64, mat:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, aq:ptr, adx:ptr, k:i64, n:i64, xs:i64, bias:ptr, act:i64)
  b0:
    tmp_sz = mul n, 256:i64
    g = alloc tmp_sz
    u = alloc tmp_sz
    a = stack 256
    cg = mul c, 2:i64
    cu = add cg, 1:i64
    call qmat_batch(cg, mat, xq, dx, g, k, n, xs)
    call qmat_batch(cu, mat, xq, dx, u, k, n, xs)
    ds = udiv xs, 2:i64
    q_off = mul c, 64:i64
    d_off = mul c, 32:i64
    jmp toks(0:i64)
  toks(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, n
    br s_more, tok_body, done
  tok_body:
    t_off = mul s, 256:i64
    gs = add g, t_off
    us = add u, t_off
    gb = mul cg, 64:i64
    call add_rows(gs, bias, gb, 64:i64)
    ub = mul cu, 64:i64
    call add_rows(us, bias, ub, 64:i64)
    call glu(gs, us, a, 64:i64, act)
    x_off = mul s, xs
    aq_s = add aq, x_off
    aq_c = add aq_s, q_off
    dd_off = mul s, ds
    adx_s = add adx, dd_off
    adx_c = add adx_s, d_off
    call quantize_q8(a, aq_c, adx_c, 64:i64)
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp toks(s2)
  done:
    free u
    free g
    ret

# moe_ffn for nb tokens (xq, dx and h rows xs, xs / 2 and 4 d bytes apart) with each token's
# results exactly moe_ffn's: every token is routed as llama_decode routes it (moe_route), the
# (token, slot) pairs are grouped by expert (moe_group) and each group's activations gathered
# (moe_gather), so each expert's gate/up and down rows run once for its group (qmat_batch, a
# row's results exactly qmat_chunk's; moe_gate_up_n, moe_down_n), and each token then adds
# its experts' outputs times their weights in the order they were picked (moe_mix_n).
# scratch holds moe_scratch_n's bytes for batches of up to nb_max tokens.
fn moe_ffn_n(h:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, nb:i64, xs:i64, router:ptr, experts:ptr, d:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64, gating:i64, scratch:ptr, router_b:ptr, act:i64, nb_max:i64, sel_b:ptr, wscale:f32)
  b0:
    logits, sel, wts, counts, offs, pairs, gx, gdx, ga, gadx, dout = call moe_buffers_n(scratch, nb_max, n_exp, n_used, fe, d)
    par nb, moe_route_tok(router, xq, dx, logits, sel, wts, d, n_exp, n_used, gating, router_b, xs, sel_b, wscale)
    call moe_group(sel, nb, n_used, n_exp, counts, offs, pairs)
    par n_exp, moe_gather(pairs, counts, offs, xq, dx, gx, gdx, xs, d, n_used)
    fchunks = udiv fe, 64:i64
    gu_tasks = mul n_exp, fchunks
    par gu_tasks, moe_gate_up_n(experts, counts, offs, gx, gdx, ga, gadx, d, fe, act)
    dchunks = udiv d, 64:i64
    dn_tasks = mul n_exp, dchunks
    par dn_tasks, moe_down_n(experts, counts, offs, pairs, ga, gadx, dout, d, fe)
    par dchunks, moe_mix_n(h, dout, wts, nb, n_used, d)
    ret

# Bytes of moe_ffn_n's scratch for batches of up to nb tokens: moe_offsets_n's buffers.
inline fn moe_scratch_n(nb:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64, d:i64)->i64
  b0:
    sel, wts, counts, offs, pairs, gx, gdx, ga, gadx, dout = call moe_offsets_n(nb, n_exp, n_used, fe, d)
    pn = mul nb, n_used
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    dout_b = mul pn, d4
    end = add dout, dout_b
    t = add end, 64:i64
    ret t

# moe_ffn_n's buffers in its scratch, for nb tokens (byte offsets; the logits at 0): each
# token's router logits and selection scores (2 rows of n_exp rounded up to 64), picked experts (i64) and their weights
# (f32); per expert its number of pairs and their first index (i64), and the pairs (token *
# n_used + slot, i64) grouped by expert; the groups' gathered activations (d int8 and d / 2
# record bytes per pair), their experts' int8 MLP activations (fe and fe / 2 bytes per
# pair), and each pair's down projection (d f32, indexed by token * n_used + slot).
inline fn moe_offsets_n(nb:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64, d:i64)->(i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64)
  b0:
    ne63 = add n_exp, 63:i64
    ne_pad = and ne63, -64:i64
    lg_row = mul ne_pad, 8:i64
    sel = mul nb, lg_row
    pn = mul nb, n_used
    p8 = mul pn, 8:i64
    wts = add sel, p8
    p4 = mul pn, 4:i64
    p4_7 = add p4, 7:i64
    p4a = and p4_7, -8:i64
    counts = add wts, p4a
    e8 = mul n_exp, 8:i64
    offs = add counts, e8
    pairs = add offs, e8
    gx = add pairs, p8
    gx_b = mul pn, d
    gdx = add gx, gx_b
    gdx_b = udiv gx_b, 2:i64
    ga = add gdx, gdx_b
    ga_b = mul pn, fe
    gadx = add ga, ga_b
    gadx_b = udiv ga_b, 2:i64
    dout0 = add gadx, gadx_b
    # f32 rows, 16-byte aligned
    dout15 = add dout0, 15:i64
    dout = and dout15, -16:i64
    ret sel, wts, counts, offs, pairs, gx, gdx, ga, gadx, dout

# moe_offsets_n's buffers as pointers into scratch.
inline fn moe_buffers_n(scratch:ptr, nb:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, fe:i64, d:i64)->(ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr)
  b0:
    o_sel, o_wts, o_counts, o_offs, o_pairs, o_gx, o_gdx, o_ga, o_gadx, o_dout = call moe_offsets_n(nb, n_exp, n_used, fe, d)
    sel = add scratch, o_sel
    wts = add scratch, o_wts
    counts = add scratch, o_counts
    offs = add scratch, o_offs
    pairs = add scratch, o_pairs
    gx = add scratch, o_gx
    gdx = add scratch, o_gdx
    ga = add scratch, o_ga
    gadx = add scratch, o_gadx
    dout = add scratch, o_dout
    ret scratch, sel, wts, counts, offs, pairs, gx, gdx, ga, gadx, dout

# Token s of a batch: moe_route on its activations into its rows of logits (2 rows of n_exp
# rounded up to 64 per token), sel and wts.
fn moe_route_tok(s:i64, router:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, logits:ptr, sel:ptr, wts:ptr, d:i64, n_exp:i64, n_used:i64, gating:i64, router_b:ptr, xs:i64, sel_b:ptr, wscale:f32)
  b0:
    ne63 = add n_exp, 63:i64
    ne_pad = and ne63, -64:i64
    lg_row = mul ne_pad, 8:i64
    lg_off = mul s, lg_row
    lg = add logits, lg_off
    su = mul s, n_used
    s8 = mul su, 8:i64
    sel_s = add sel, s8
    s4 = mul su, 4:i64
    wts_s = add wts, s4
    x_off = mul s, xs
    xq_s = add xq, x_off
    ds = udiv xs, 2:i64
    d_off = mul s, ds
    dx_s = add dx, d_off
    call moe_route(router, xq_s, dx_s, lg, sel_s, wts_s, d, n_exp, n_used, gating, router_b, sel_b, wscale)
    ret

# The nb tokens' picks grouped by expert: counts[e] pairs (token * n_used + slot) picked e,
# at pairs[offs[e] ..], in token then slot order.
fn moe_group(sel:ptr, nb:i64, n_used:i64, n_exp:i64, counts:ptr, offs:ptr, pairs:ptr)
  b0:
    pn = mul nb, n_used
    jmp clear(0:i64)
  clear(e:i64):
    e_more = lt e, n_exp
    br e_more, clear_body, count(0:i64)
  clear_body:
    st counts[e], 0:i64
    e2 = add e, 1:i64
    jmp clear(e2)
  count(i:i64):
    i_more = lt i, pn
    br i_more, count_body, prefix(0:i64, 0:i64)
  count_body:
    x = ld sel[i]:i64
    cx = ld counts[x]:i64
    cx2 = add cx, 1:i64
    st counts[x], cx2
    i2 = add i, 1:i64
    jmp count(i2)
  # offs = the counts' exclusive prefix sums; counts then serve as each group's fill cursor
  # (back to the counts once filled).
  prefix(pe:i64, acc:i64):
    pe_more = lt pe, n_exp
    br pe_more, prefix_body, fill_start
  prefix_body:
    st offs[pe], acc
    cp = ld counts[pe]:i64
    acc2 = add acc, cp
    st counts[pe], 0:i64
    pe2 = add pe, 1:i64
    jmp prefix(pe2, acc2)
  fill_start:
    jmp fill(0:i64)
  fill(j:i64):
    j_more = lt j, pn
    br j_more, fill_body, done
  fill_body:
    y = ld sel[j]:i64
    oy = ld offs[y]:i64
    cy = ld counts[y]:i64
    at = add oy, cy
    st pairs[at], j
    cy2 = add cy, 1:i64
    st counts[y], cy2
    j2 = add j, 1:i64
    jmp fill(j2)
  done:
    ret

# Expert e's group: each pair's token's int8 activations (d bytes from xq, xs apart) and
# block records (d / 2 bytes from dx) into the group's rows of gx and gdx.
fn moe_gather(e:i64, pairs:ptr, counts:ptr, offs:ptr, xq:ptr, dx:ptr, gx:ptr, gdx:ptr, xs:i64, d:i64, n_used:i64)
  b0:
    cnt = ld counts[e]:i64
    off = ld offs[e]:i64
    ds = udiv xs, 2:i64
    d2 = udiv d, 2:i64
    jmp loop(0:i64)
  loop(p:i64):
    more = lt p, cnt
    br more, body, done
  body:
    at = add off, p
    pr = ld pairs[at]:i64
    tok = udiv pr, n_used
    src_off = mul tok, xs
    src = add xq, src_off
    dst_off = mul at, d
    dst = add gx, dst_off
    call copy_f32(src, dst, d)
    srd_off = mul tok, ds
    srd = add dx, srd_off
    dsd_off = mul at, d2
    dsd = add gdx, dsd_off
    call copy_f32(srd, dsd, d2)
    p2 = add p, 1:i64
    jmp loop(p2)
  done:
    ret

# Task t of the grouped expert MLPs: rows 64c..64c+63 of expert e's gate/up (t = e * fe/64 +
# c) for its group's tokens (qmat_batch on the gathered activations), their bias and the
# activation, then Q8 quantization into the group's rows of ga/gadx, as gate_up does for
# one token.
fn moe_gate_up_n(t:i64, experts:ptr, counts:ptr, offs:ptr, gx:ptr, gdx:ptr, ga:ptr, gadx:ptr, d:i64, fe:i64, act:i64)
  b0:
    fchunks = udiv fe, 64:i64
    e = udiv t, fchunks
    c = urem t, fchunks
    cnt = ld counts[e]:i64
    none = eq cnt, 0:i64
    br none, done, run
  run:
    off = ld offs[e]:i64
    e4 = mul e, 4:i64
    mat = ld experts[e4]:ptr
    e42 = add e4, 2:i64
    bias = ld experts[e42]:ptr
    x_off = mul off, d
    gx_e = add gx, x_off
    d2 = udiv d, 2:i64
    xd_off = mul off, d2
    gdx_e = add gdx, xd_off
    tmp_sz = mul cnt, 256:i64
    g = alloc tmp_sz
    u = alloc tmp_sz
    a = stack 256
    cg = mul c, 2:i64
    cu = add cg, 1:i64
    call qmat_batch(cg, mat, gx_e, gdx_e, g, d, cnt, d)
    call qmat_batch(cu, mat, gx_e, gdx_e, u, d, cnt, d)
    gb = mul cg, 64:i64
    ub = mul cu, 64:i64
    q_c = mul c, 64:i64
    d_c = mul c, 32:i64
    fe2 = udiv fe, 2:i64
    jmp toks(0:i64)
  toks(p:i64):
    p_more = lt p, cnt
    br p_more, tok_body, free_tmp
  tok_body:
    r_off = mul p, 256:i64
    gs = add g, r_off
    us = add u, r_off
    call add_rows(gs, bias, gb, 64:i64)
    call add_rows(us, bias, ub, 64:i64)
    call glu(gs, us, a, 64:i64, act)
    at = add off, p
    aq_off0 = mul at, fe
    aq_off = add aq_off0, q_c
    aq_p = add ga, aq_off
    ad_off0 = mul at, fe2
    ad_off = add ad_off0, d_c
    ad_p = add gadx, ad_off
    call quantize_q8(a, aq_p, ad_p, 64:i64)
    p2 = add p, 1:i64
    jmp toks(p2)
  free_tmp:
    free u
    free g
    jmp done
  done:
    ret

# Task t of the grouped down projections: rows 64c..64c+63 of expert e's down (t = e * d/64 +
# c) for its group's tokens (qmat_batch on their MLP activations), plus its bias, into each
# pair's row of dout.
fn moe_down_n(t:i64, experts:ptr, counts:ptr, offs:ptr, pairs:ptr, ga:ptr, gadx:ptr, dout:ptr, d:i64, fe:i64)
  b0:
    dchunks = udiv d, 64:i64
    e = udiv t, dchunks
    c = urem t, dchunks
    cnt = ld counts[e]:i64
    none = eq cnt, 0:i64
    br none, done, run
  run:
    off = ld offs[e]:i64
    e4 = mul e, 4:i64
    e41 = add e4, 1:i64
    mat = ld experts[e41]:ptr
    e43 = add e4, 3:i64
    bias = ld experts[e43]:ptr
    a_off = mul off, fe
    ga_e = add ga, a_off
    fe2 = udiv fe, 2:i64
    ad_off = mul off, fe2
    gadx_e = add gadx, ad_off
    tmp_sz = mul cnt, 256:i64
    tmp = alloc tmp_sz
    call qmat_batch(c, mat, ga_e, gadx_e, tmp, fe, cnt, fe)
    b_off = mul c, 64:i64
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    c_off = mul c, 256:i64
    jmp toks(0:i64)
  toks(p:i64):
    p_more = lt p, cnt
    br p_more, tok_body, free_tmp
  tok_body:
    r_off = mul p, 256:i64
    row = add tmp, r_off
    call add_rows(row, bias, b_off, 64:i64)
    at = add off, p
    pr = ld pairs[at]:i64
    o_off0 = mul pr, d4
    o_off = add o_off0, c_off
    o = add dout, o_off
    call copy_f32(row, o, 256:i64)
    p2 = add p, 1:i64
    jmp toks(p2)
  free_tmp:
    free tmp
    jmp done
  done:
    ret

# Rows 64c..64c+63 of each of the nb tokens' residual streams (4 d bytes apart) += the sum
# over its picked experts, in the order they were picked, of each one's weight times its
# down projection (dout's row of the pair), as moe_down adds them.
fn moe_mix_n(c:i64, h:ptr, dout:ptr, wts:ptr, nb:i64, n_used:i64, d:i64)
  b0:
    w = vl f32
    acc = stack 256
    zero = splat 0.0:f32:vx
    d4 = mul d, 4:i64
    c_off = mul c, 256:i64
    jmp toks(0:i64)
  toks(s:i64):
    s_more = lt s, nb
    br s_more, clear(0:i64), done
  clear(j:i64):
    j_more = lt j, 64:i64
    br j_more, clear_body, slots(0:i64)
  clear_body:
    j_rest = sub 64:i64, j
    stm acc[j], zero, j_rest:f32
    j2 = add j, w
    jmp clear(j2)
  slots(k:i64):
    k_more = lt k, n_used
    br k_more, slot_body, add_h(0:i64)
  slot_body:
    su = mul s, n_used
    pr = add su, k
    ws = ld wts[pr]:f32
    vw = splat ws:vx
    o_off0 = mul pr, d4
    o_off = add o_off0, c_off
    o = add dout, o_off
    jmp mix(0:i64)
  mix(m:i64):
    m_more = lt m, 64:i64
    br m_more, mix_body, slot_next
  mix_body:
    m_rest = sub 64:i64, m
    tv = ldm o[m]:vx, m_rest:f32
    av = ldm acc[m]:vx, m_rest:f32
    nv = vfma tv, vw, av:f32
    stm acc[m], nv, m_rest:f32
    m2 = add m, w
    jmp mix(m2)
  slot_next:
    k2 = add k, 1:i64
    jmp slots(k2)
  add_h(a:i64):
    a_more = lt a, 64:i64
    br a_more, add_body, tok_next
  add_body:
    a_rest = sub 64:i64, a
    h_row0 = mul s, d4
    h_row = add h, h_row0
    hc = add h_row, c_off
    acv = ldm acc[a]:vx, a_rest:f32
    hv = ldm hc[a]:vx, a_rest:f32
    sum = vadd hv, acv:f32
    stm hc[a], sum, a_rest:f32
    a2 = add a, w
    jmp add_h(a2)
  tok_next:
    s2 = add s, 1:i64
    jmp toks(s2)
  done:
    ret

# The 9 words of cfg: d, layers, heads, kv_heads, head_dim, ffn, vocab, max_ctx and the KV
# cache's format (0 bf16, 1 int8); max_ctx rounded up to a multiple of 32, the cache's
# positions per head (it is stored in tiles of 32 positions).
inline fn load_cfg(cfg:ptr)->(i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64, i64)
  b0:
    d = ld cfg[0]:i64
    nl = ld cfg[1]:i64
    nh = ld cfg[2]:i64
    nkv = ld cfg[3]:i64
    hd = ld cfg[4]:i64
    f = ld cfg[5]:i64
    vocab = ld cfg[6]:i64
    ctx = ld cfg[7]:i64
    ctx31 = add ctx, 31:i64
    max_ctx = and ctx31, -32:i64
    kvf = ld cfg[8]:i64
    ret d, nl, nh, nkv, hd, f, vocab, max_ctx, kvf

# Bytes per position of a KV head's K (or V) in the cache: hd bf16 values, or hd int8 values
# and an f32 scale (kvf 1).
inline fn kv_rb(hd:i64, kvf:i64)->i64
  b0:
    is_q8 = eq kvf, 1:i64
    q8b = add hd, 4:i64
    bf = shl hd, 1:i64
    rb = select is_q8, q8b, bf
    ret rb

# The cache of a layer whose queries see the last win positions (0: all of them): its
# positions per KV head, ctx_l, and its ring. With a window, when that is smaller than
# max_ctx, a ring of R = win + 31 + 256 slots rounded up to 32 holds position p at slot p mod
# R and again at p mod R + R (ctx_l = 2 R): a window read from its first tile (up to win + 31
# positions) or a prefill's shared split (256) is then one run of slots, and a prefill piece
# of up to 256 tokens (llama_prefill) writes its K and V without overwriting a position its
# own windows read. Otherwise ctx_l = max_ctx and ring 0, slot p for position p.
inline fn kv_ring(win:i64, max_ctx:i64)->(i64, i64)
  b0:
    r0 = add win, 318:i64
    r = and r0, -32:i64
    two = shl r, 1:i64
    windowed = ne win, 0:i64
    fits = lt two, max_ctx
    use = and windowed, fits
    ring = select use, r, 0:i64
    ctx_l = select use, two, max_ctx
    ret ctx_l, ring

# Position p's slot: p mod ring, or p without a ring (0).
inline fn ring_slot(p:i64, ring:i64)->i64
  b0:
    has = ne ring, 0:i64
    rdiv = select has, ring, 9223372036854775807:i64
    s = urem p, rdiv
    ret s

# The model table's global entries: embedding, final norm, LM head, RoPE cos and sin
# tables.
inline fn model_globals(model:ptr)->(ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr)
  b0:
    embd = ld model[0]:ptr
    norm_out = ld model[1]:ptr
    lm = ld model[2]:ptr
    cos_t = ld model[3]:ptr
    sin_t = ld model[4]:ptr
    ret embd, norm_out, lm, cos_t, sin_t

# Layer l's entries (the first 15 of its 18 words at 5 + 18 l; layer_shared reads the rest): its two norm weights, its QKV, O, gate/up and
# down matrices, its q and k head norm weights (0 for none), a mixture-of-experts layer's
# router and expert table (0 for a dense layer), its QKV, O and router biases and attention
# sinks (0 for none), and its attention window in positions (0 for all of them).
inline fn layer_weights(model:ptr, l:i64)->(ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, ptr, i64)
  b0:
    slot0 = mul l, 18:i64
    slot = add slot0, 5:i64
    lp_off = shl slot, 3:i64
    lp = add model, lp_off
    attn_norm = ld lp[0]:ptr
    m_qkv = ld lp[1]:ptr
    m_o = ld lp[2]:ptr
    ffn_norm = ld lp[3]:ptr
    m_gu = ld lp[4]:ptr
    m_dn = ld lp[5]:ptr
    q_norm = ld lp[6]:ptr
    k_norm = ld lp[7]:ptr
    router = ld lp[8]:ptr
    experts = ld lp[9]:ptr
    qkv_b = ld lp[10]:ptr
    o_b = ld lp[11]:ptr
    router_b = ld lp[12]:ptr
    sinks = ld lp[13]:ptr
    win = ld lp[14]:i64
    ret attn_norm, m_qkv, m_o, ffn_norm, m_gu, m_dn, q_norm, k_norm, router, experts, qkv_b, o_b, router_b, sinks, win

# cfg's words 11 and 14-16: an expert's MLP width, the rotary dimensions of a head (0 for
# all hd; GLM-4.5 rotates half), the shared experts' MLP width (0 for none) and the routed
# experts' weight scale (an f32 in the word's low 4 bytes).
inline fn load_ext(cfg:ptr, hd:i64)->(i64, i64, i64, f32)
  b0:
    fe = ld cfg[11]:i64
    rd0 = ld cfg[14]:i64
    none = eq rd0, 0:i64
    rd = select none, hd, rd0
    fs = ld cfg[15]:i64
    wscale = ld cfg[16:i64]:f32
    ret fe, rd, fs, wscale

# Layer l's DeepSeek-style entries (words 15-17 of its 18): its shared expert's gate/up and
# down matrices (0 for none), and its routed experts' selection bias f32 [experts] (0 for
# none).
inline fn layer_shared(model:ptr, l:i64)->(ptr, ptr, ptr)
  b0:
    slot0 = mul l, 18:i64
    slot = add slot0, 5:i64
    lp_off = shl slot, 3:i64
    lp = add model, lp_off
    sgu = ld lp[15]:ptr
    sdn = ld lp[16]:ptr
    selb = ld lp[17]:ptr
    ret sgu, sdn, selb

# cfg's mixture-of-experts and MLP words: the experts, the experts each token uses, how
# their weights are made (moe_route's gating: 0 softmax probabilities, 1 renormalized, 2 a
# softmax of the picked logits; cfg[11], an expert's MLP width, is ffn's place in cfg[5]),
# and the MLP's activation (glu: 0 SwiGLU, 1 gpt-oss's clamped SwiGLU).
inline fn load_moe(cfg:ptr)->(i64, i64, i64, i64)
  b0:
    n_exp = ld cfg[9]:i64
    n_used = ld cfg[10]:i64
    gating = ld cfg[12]:i64
    act = ld cfg[13]:i64
    ret n_exp, n_used, gating, act
